29CFR 1910.119. The following accident prevention program elements are in place at the North Muskegon Terminal:

1) Employee Participation,
2) Process Safety Information,
3) Process Hazard Analyses (PHAs),
4) Standard Operating Procedures,
5) Operator and Maintenance Training,
6) Contractor Management and Evaluations,
7) Pre-startup Safety Reviews,
8) Mechanical Integrity with Performance Testing/Preventive Maintenance
9) Safe Work Permits,
10) Management of Change,
11) Accident/Process Safety Event Investigation,
12) Emergency Planning and Response,
13) Internal and Regulatory Compliance Audits, and
14) Trade Secrets.

These fourteen (14) individual elements of the prevention program work together to prevent accidental chemical releases. MPLX and its employees are committed to the standards required by these management programs. In addition to the above elements, there are also specific prevention measures that are employed as part of the Terminal's operating procedures and engineering/administrative controls to help quickly detect, contain/control and reduce the consequences of a release. These are briefly summarized as follows:

General Risk Reduction and Safety Measures

-Engineering and construction in accordance with recognized industry and company standards (ex. NFPA 58.);
-Equipment properly designed with protection from overpressure (pressure safety relief valves, etc.);
-Updated technical drawings, Piping & Instrumentation Diagrams and Process Flow Diagrams;
-Operating systems monitored and controlled by trained personnel along with 24/7 remote monitoring;
-Redundant automated control systems;
-Automatic and manual shutdown devices for critical systems;
-Scheduled inspection and testing of instruments, butane-containing components, and safety devices;
-Controlled/secured facility access;
-Regular safety meetings and safety awareness programs;
-Routinely scheduled safety inspections and audits;
-Frequent unit surveillance by operators.

